course: dictionary
lesson: 14537
title: A grand word for a person
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Personage is a formal word for a person, usually one who is important or famous. «The mayor was a personage whom everyone in town wanted to meet.» The word sounds grand, so you know this person matters. Use the words around it as clues.
explain: Personage has a second meaning: a character in a play or story. «Alice meets many odd personages in Wonderland, such as the King and Queen of Hearts.» Wonderland is a story, so personages here means characters, not real important people.
explain: Writers sometimes use personage with a little smile, to make someone sound grander than they really are. «Toad thinks of himself as an important personage.» The word is a joke here, because Toad is very vain. Check the clues before you decide what the word means.
fact: Personage is a noun, and its plural is personages.
fact: «Personage» means an important or famous person.
fact: «Personage» can also mean a character in a play or story.
fact: Personage is a formal word, used in older stories and serious writing.
fact: To check your meaning, swap in «important person» or «character»: if it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
exercise: «The guest was a personage, so the crowd made way for her.» What does personage mean here? | A quiet whisper | A kind of tree | *An important person | A small animal
exercise: «Alice meets many odd personages in Wonderland.» In this sentence, what are the personages? | Rain clouds | Plants that grow in the garden | Ancient castles | *Characters in a story
exercise: What is the plural of personage? | personaged | personage | personagies | *personages
test: «The king was a great personage in the land, and every lord bowed to him.» Why does the author call the king a personage? | *Because he was an important person | Because he was lost | Because he was a mouse | Because he was asleep
test: «The play had five personages, and each wore a mask.» What does personage mean in this line? | Old buildings | Rainy days | Important guests | *Characters in the play
exam: «The mayor, a respected personage, opened the new library.» What does the author tell us about the mayor? | The mayor is a character in a play | *The mayor is an important person | The mayor is a tree | The mayor is lost
